And dim is the forest track;
But the sportsman Death comes striding on:
Brothers, the way is black.

spout:
Strange winged dragons writhe about
These vases, poisoned venoms spout,
Impregnate with old Chinese charms;

spoils:
With pensive mind I search the drear abode,
Where the great conqu'ror has his spoils bestow'd;
There where the offspring of six thousand years

spotless:
She wouldn't put powder upon her nose;
And petticoats sheltered her spotless hose;
She knew how to market and mend and sweep;

spouse:
Where heav'n's Supreme in bliss and glory reigns.
There sits, illustrious Sir, thy beauteous spouse;
A gem-blaz'd circle beaming on her brows.

spooned:
A pewter age,—mixed metal, silver-washed;
An age of scum, spooned off the richer past;
An age of patches for old gaberdines;
